<section class="hero wrap"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="kicker">A COMMUNITY TAKING ROOT · PLANNED FOR 2027</p><h1>There’s more here <br/>than meets <br/><em>the eye.</em></h1><p class="lead">In familiar woods. Under the neighborhood oaks. In the questions we haven’t learned to ask yet.</p><p>NeoMyco is a new community taking shape in Northeast Ohio. We’re bringing people together to explore fungi, learn field mycology, and make observations that others can build on.</p><a class="button" href="#in-the-field">Open the field notebook <span>↓</span></a><p class="margin-note">Bring your curiosity. We’ll learn together.</p></div><figure class="specimen hero-plate"><div class="plate-head"><span>FIELD RECORD / 001</span><span>SUMMIT COUNTY, OHIO</span></div><img src="https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/314765196/large.jpg" alt="Inocybe communis photographed in Donn Bialik’s front yard in 2023" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption><span class="hand-note">A discovery close to home.</span><h2><i>Inocybe communis</i></h2><div class="label-grid"><span>OBSERVED<strong>28 AUG 2023</strong></span><span>OBSERVER<strong>DONN BIALIK / MYCOGEEKY</strong></span></div><p>Two small mushrooms near mature white oaks. An observation later cited in a species description.</p><a href="#field-record">Follow this collection’s story ↓</a></figcaption></figure></section>
<div class="principles wrap"><span>Explore</span><span>Learn</span><span>Document</span><span>Contribute</span></div>
<section class="wrap section" id="in-the-field"><div class="section-heading"><p class="kicker">01 / THE COMMUNITY WE’RE BUILDING</p><h2>A walk in the woods. <br/><em>A place for your questions.</em></h2></div><div class="intro"><p class="lead">MycoView’s curiosity, put into practice. Outdoors, around a collection table, and alongside people who want to keep learning.</p><p>Our planned forays and workshops will connect the pleasure of finding mushrooms with ecology, careful collections, iNaturalist, microscopy, and DNA evidence. You can come for a richer afternoon in the woods, or follow a question further. Both belong here.</p></div><div class="practice-grid">{practices.map(([n,title,body])=><article><span class="number">{n}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></article>)}</div><aside class="note"><strong>A next step, within reach.</strong><p>We’re developing practical training and opportunities to learn alongside more experienced naturalists. Bring an interest, a skill, or a question—and help shape what we explore together.</p></aside></section>
<section class="case-section" id="field-record"><div class="wrap section"><p class="kicker">02 / A REAL EXAMPLE · FROM THE FOUNDER’S FIELDWORK</p><div class="section-heading"><h2>From the front yard <br/><em>to the scientific record.</em></h2><p class="lead">A familiar place can hold an unfamiliar species.</p></div><div class="case-layout"><figure class="specimen"><div class="plate-head"><span>OBSERVATION 180676766</span><span>28.08.2023</span></div><img src="https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/314765219/large.jpg" alt="Another view from Donn’s 2023 Inocybe communis collection" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><h3>A record worth keeping.</h3><p>Donn’s field notes place these mushrooms near three large white oaks (<i>Quercus alba</i>). The record links photographs, habitat notes, and an ITS DNA barcode.</p><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/180676766">Explore the original observation ↗</a></figcaption></figure><div class="record-story"><article><p class="kicker">I / NOTICE & DOCUMENT</p><h3>It started in the front yard.</h3><p>On August 28, 2023, Donn Bialik documented two small mushrooms at home. Careful records gave the find a life beyond the day it was collected.</p></article><article><p class="kicker">II / A WORKING IDENTITY</p><h3>A name with a question still attached.</h3><p>The observation’s history includes <i>Inocybe</i> sp. “radiata-IN01”: a provisional label used to keep track of a lineage while its identity was investigated. Its sequence is recorded in GenBank as <a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/nuccore/PP850762">PP850762 ↗</a>.</p></article><article><p class="kicker">III / SHARED KNOWLEDGE</p><h3><i>Inocybe communis.</i> Formally described.</h3><p>In 2026, Sigrid Jakob, Scott Ostuni, Kyle Canan, Linas V. Kudzma, and P. Brandon Matheny published descriptions of six new species of Inocybaceae, including this one.</p><p>Donn’s 2023 observation is cited among representative iNaturalist records with molecular annotations. The authors explicitly distinguish these records from specimens they examined directly.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://doi.org/10.1080/00275514.2026.2685369">Read the research paper ↗</a></article></div></div><div class="return-record"><img src="https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/715327092/large.jpg" alt="Inocybe communis observed again on Donn’s property in August 2026" loading="lazy"/><div><p class="kicker">IV / RETURN TO THE SAME PLACE</p><h3>The story keeps growing.</h3><p>A second front-yard observation, made August 11, 2026, is also identified as <i>Inocybe communis</i> and has its own DNA barcode. Revisiting a familiar place gives us more opportunities to notice, compare, and ask questions.</p><a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/390447468">See the 2026 observation ↗</a></div></div><p class="source-note">Photographs and observations: Donn Bialik (MycoGeeky). These records predate NeoMyco’s launch. Sigrid, Scott, and Kyle are friends of Donn; Scott and Sigrid are also involved in the Amateur Mycology Publishing Group. Their collaborative work helps inspire what we’re building.</p></div></section>
<section class="wrap section woods"><div><p class="kicker">03 / KNOW YOUR WOODS</p><h2>One place. <br/>Many visits. <br/><em>More to discover.</em></h2></div><div><p class="lead">What fungi live in a place you already know?</p><p>A favorite park. A patch of woodland. Your own yard. Know Your Woods is our developing invitation to return, observe, and build a useful record of fungal life over time.</p><p>You can begin with a camera, a notebook, and somewhere you’re allowed to explore.</p><a class="button" href="/neo-myco/know-your-woods/">Begin with a familiar place <span>→</span></a></div></section>
<section class="join wrap"><p class="kicker">THE NEXT PAGE IS STILL UNWRITTEN</p><h2>There’s room for <br/><em>your curiosity here.</em></h2><p>We’re preparing for a 2027 launch. Forays, workshops, and collaborative projects are taking shape. Interested in participating, sharing a skill, or helping build the community?</p><a class="button" href="https://www.inaturalist.org/people/mycogeekyohio">Get in touch on iNaturalist <span>↗</span></a><small>Dates and program details will be shared as they are confirmed.</small></section>
